  "description": "HABDUN crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/m. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H86 N4 Ni4 O34 Yb4 2+,2(N1 O3 1-),24(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni2 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni3 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni4 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 8 O neighbors; Ni5 (Ni) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 14 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.146-4.040 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.40-134.30°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C60H134Yb4N6Ni4O64. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
